{"id": "EUVD-2026-88015", "enisaUuid": "d99079cc-a24c-36e4-98c5-33dc7da1879b", "description": "The OCI delta stream parser read sizes as guint64 but passed them to GLib I/O and allocation functions expecting gsize (32 bits on 32-bit systems), causing undersized allocations while subsequent operations use the original 64-bit size, leading to heap buffer overflows. An attacker controlling an OCI registry can craft a delta stream that triggers this during flatpak install/update, potentially achieving code execution on 32-bit systems.", "datePublished": "2026-09-27T20:19:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T16:25:45", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80497", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80498", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80687", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-96280", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2539419", "https://github.com/flatpak/flatpak/security/advisories/GHSA-jr92-2v97-wgvc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-96280"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "130bdabc-c12d-3c03-9782-b614ac906d1c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.12.9-4.el9_8.4"}, {"id": "9506d30d-405d-3138-ae5c-ebd4e9b89163", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.12.9-7.el8_10"}, {"id": "f87d9c89-7755-3b44-bd51-557a51a6d314", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.16.0-9.el10_2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "46efe89e-40de-3081-8b87-172a541b1b98", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}